# png-every: 5
# intro: 1
# what: The opening demo (opdemo.bin) from boot, no save (#34): the prologue over the pendant, the demon's warning, the title screen with ttl2's ornament growing in and the sand dissolves, the credits, the storm demo (fifteen pictures with the typed story, the throne-room dialogue, the doorway epilogue), to the hand-back that loads the town.  The oracle runs with ORACLE_INTRO=1 (it does not tap Return to skip the demo; tracing starts at opdemo's entry 6002), the port with `--intro`.  Boundary site `intro:wait`, one per completed wait (the same sites as the ending's `end:wait`, HARNESS.md s6): 7439 of them, no input.  The picture at every boundary is the evidence; found and fixed with it: the storm demo's demon-eye frames had planes 1 and 2 swapped (6EC7/6ECC), the stencil laying them over hime.grp (6ED8) is built from the destination at (19,24), the narrator's ink and shadow start at 0 (the script's first 'P' is black), the epilogue (yuu3's third plane 6FAC, yuu4's stencil 6F41) was never reached because the last NARR() mistook the script's 0xFF for an abort.
.7500
